<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">21 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 21 November, from 235 to 1995.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/bishop" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bishop.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">235 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,791 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Anterus succeeds Pontian as bishop of Rome</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Anterus became the nineteenth pope, succeeding Pontian, who had been arrested and sent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> during the persecution of Christians under Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maximinus-thrax">Maximinus Thrax</a>. Anterus died on 3 January 236.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">Papacy</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1620">1620 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">406 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mayflower passengers sign the Mayflower Compact</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Anchored off <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-cod">Cape Cod</a>, 41 male passengers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mayflower">Mayflower</a> signed a compact binding themselves into a 'civil body politic'. The agreement became an early landmark of self-government by consent in English America.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1783">1783 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">243 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Two Frenchmen make the first free flight in a balloon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Pilâtre de Rozier and the Marquis d'Arlandes rose from the Bois de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boulogne-sur-mer">Boulogne</a> in a Montgolfier hot-air balloon and drifted about 9 kilometres across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> in 25 minutes, the first untethered human flight.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1789">1789 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">237 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">North Carolina becomes the 12th US state</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">North Carolina ratified the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitution-of-the-united-states">Constitution of the United States</a> and was admitted as the 12th state. The Constitution, drafted by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitutional-convention-united-states">Philadelphia Convention</a> in 1787, had replaced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/articles-of-confederation">Articles of Confederation</a> in March 1789.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitution-of-the-united-states">US Constitution</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1877">1877 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">149 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edison announces his phonograph</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Thomas Edison announced his invention of the phonograph, a machine that recorded sound on tinfoil and played it back. It was the first device able to reproduce the human voice.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1894">1894 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">132 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Japanese troops take Port Arthur and begin a massacre</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After capturing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lushunkou">Lüshunkou</a>, known to Europeans as Port Arthur, advance troops of the Japanese Second Army began three days of killing in the city. Estimates of the dead range from 2,600 civilians to 20,000 people, including Chinese soldiers.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-sino-japanese-war">First Sino-Japanese War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lushunkou">Lüshunkou</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1920">1920 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">106 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bloody Sunday in Dublin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michael-collins">Michael Collins</a>'s IRA squad killed 14 men, mostly British intelligence officers, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a> that morning. In the afternoon, Crown forces fired on the crowd at a Gaelic football match in Croke Park, killing 14 civilians.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1995">1995 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">31 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Dayton Agreement is initialled, ending the Bosnian War</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After three weeks of talks at an air base in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ohio">Ohio</a>, the leaders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> initialled a peace agreement. The war had killed about 100,000 people, including some 8,000 at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srebrenica">Srebrenica</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 21 November <span class="n">2</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/voltaire"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/voltaire.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Voltaire</span><span class="tp">1694–1778</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/rene-magritte"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/rene-magritte.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">René Magritte</span><span class="tp">1898–1967</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 21 November <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/garcia-ramirez-of-navarre"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/garcia-ramirez-of-navarre.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">García Ramírez of Navarre</span><span class="tp">c. 1112–1150</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/yury-of-moscow"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Yury of Moscow</span><span class="tp">1281–1325</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/georgius-agricola"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/georgius-agricola.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Georgius Agricola</span><span class="tp">1494–1555</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/heinrich-von-kleist"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/heinrich-von-kleist.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Heinrich von Kleist</span><span class="tp">1777–1811</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/j-b-m-hertzog"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/j-b-m-hertzog.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">J. B. M. Hertzog</span><span class="tp">1866–1942</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/francis-burton-harrison"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francis-burton-harrison.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Francis Burton Harrison</span><span class="tp">1873–1957</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/kaysone-phomvihane"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Kaysone Phomvihane</span><span class="tp">1920–1992</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/hassan-gouled-aptidon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hassan-gouled-aptidon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Hassan Gouled Aptidon</span><span class="tp">1916–2006</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
